COMPILATION OF: E49D1

D: Disk Print
L: List Source Program

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 1

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 2

PL/I-80 V1.4 COMPILATION OF: E49D1

   1 a 0000 E49D1:
   2 a 0006   procedure options(main);
   3 a 0006   /* [E2E-49/P3] member-vs-member compare, BARE LEFT and QUALIFIED
   4 a 0006      RIGHT (`na = rec.nb'), equal extents.  E49B1 measured the
   5 a 0006      qualified-qualified head `21 *D(left) / E5 / 21 *D(right) / D1
   6 a 0006      / 06 03 / 78 / CD ?SCCCM'; [C335] proved the [C253]/[C258]
   7 a 0006      fold invisible to the encoding member-LEFT-of-literal.  If the
   8 a 0006      fold is invisible here too the object equals E49B1 byte for
   9 a 0006      byte but the module-name bytes; a PASS-2 refusal would be a
  10 a 0006      new dr-refuses boundary. */
  11 c 0006   dcl
  12 c 0006     1 rec,
  13 c 0006       2 na char(3),
  14 c 0006       2 nb char(3),
  15 c 0006       2 s2 char(2);
  16 c 0006   dcl k fixed bin(15);
  17 c 0006   if na = rec.nb then k = 1;
  18 c 001D   put list('K=', k);
  19 c 003F   stop;
  20 a 0042 end E49D1;

CODE SIZE = 0042
DATA AREA = 000C
FREE SYMS = 3888
END  COMPILATION
